<title>GERMANY: Heidelberger Druck profits up in '96/97.</title>
<headline>Heidelberger Druck profits up in '96/97.</headline>
<dateline>HEIDELBERG, Germany 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31.</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>					     1996/97	    1995/96</p>
<p>    Group net profit			 353	 vs 268</p>
<p>    Group income from ord. activities  704	 vs 572</p>
<p>    Group sales			    5,057	 vs 4,286</p>
<p>    DVFA earnings per share (marks)  85.73	 vs 61.43</p>
<p>    Parent net profit			270	 vs 205</p>
<p>    Parent income from ord. activites  574	 vs 507</p>
<p>    Parent sales			   3,118	 vs 2,905</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German printing group is Heidelberger Druckmaschinen AG, which is controlled by utility RWE AG. Net profit figure has tax effects of special dividend stripped out. The company proposed a 1996/97 dividend of 28 percent, after a 22 percent dividend with a nine percent bonus in the previous year.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
